# Gitignored files a NEW worktree needs to run, copied from the checkout it
# was created from. Read by Claude Code (`--worktree`, subagent and desktop
# worktrees) and by the Codex app (Codex-managed worktrees); `.gitignore`
# syntax, and only files that are ALSO gitignored are copied, so a tracked file
# is never duplicated. `bun run worktree:provision` covers every other kind of
# worktree (orchestrated, `git worktree add`) and copies the same files: the
# shipped lines below mirror `PROVISION_COPIES` in `cli/lib/worktree.ts`, and a
# test keeps the two equal.
#
# What this file cannot carry: `node_modules/`, the `.husky/_` hook shims and
# the `.claude/skills` alias. Without them git hooks do not run and Claude Code
# finds no repo skill; the prompt hook says so, and `bun run worktree:provision`
# (the Codex app runs it from `.codex/environments/environment.toml`) adds them.
#
# Shared with the team: list only what a fresh worktree cannot rebuild. Add a
# project-only line below the shipped ones; the updater delivers this file once
# and never overwrites it.

# Values every harness launch and every MCP loader read, and their overrides.
.env
.env.local
# Claude Code's local settings (permissions, approved MCP servers).
.claude/settings.local.json
# The curl token and browser state from `bun run api:login`. Never the
# plaintext MCP credential copies the .env loader retired (ADR-0011).
.auth/**
!.auth/opencode/**
!.auth/harness-env-backup/**
# `bun run api:sync` config: without it `api:sync -c` falls into prompts.
api/.openapi-config.json
# The synced OpenAPI spec: the OpenAPI MCP exits at start without it when
# OPENAPI_SPEC_PATH points here (`bun run api:sync` rebuilds it).
api/openapi.json
# Per-developer MCP overrides.
.mcp.local.json
opencode.local.jsonc
dbhub.local.toml
# The installer's record of community skills (`setup:doctor` reads it).
.template/installer.state.json
